Adapted parts. Each file names its source and its changes in its header.

- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/oauth.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/oauth.rs: the authorization URL, the code
  exchange, the token refresh, userinfo, and the rule that refreshes a token
  only when it has less than 300 seconds left.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/client.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/oauth.rs: the client's key name
  (antigravity_enterprise) and the single client it logs in with, read here
  from oauth-client.json.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/oauth_server.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/oauth_server.rs: the loopback callback server,
  the state check, the request limits, the 10-minute wait and the pasted
  callback URL.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/token.rs
  from src-tauri/src/models/token.rs: the token record.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/index.rs
  from src-tauri/src/models/account.rs and src-tauri/src/modules/account.rs:
  the account index layout (accounts.json, version 2.0) and the account id.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/login.rs
  follows the order of start_oauth_login in src-tauri/src/commands/oauth.rs
  and the invalid_grant handling in src-tauri/src/modules/account.rs.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/cloud_code.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/quota.rs: the Cloud Code hosts and their
  choice, the loadCodeAssist request and its metadata, the
  fetchAvailableModels and retrieveUserQuotaSummary requests and the payload
  cached from them, the 403 handling, the retries a second apart, and the
  reading of Google's error bodies and verification links.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/version.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/wakeup_gateway.rs and
  src-tauri/src/modules/quota.rs: where Antigravity's version is read
  (product.json, Info.plist through plutil, google-auth-library), the user
  agents, x-goog-api-client, the platform name and the defaults.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/export.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/quota.rs: the quota cache record, its file name
  (the SHA-256 of the email), its folder and its 60-second TTL.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/quota.rs
  follows the order of fetch_quota_with_fresh_token in
  src-tauri/src/modules/account.rs and fetch_quota_with_context in
  src-tauri/src/modules/quota.rs, and their handling of 403, invalid_grant
  and verification requests.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/credential.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/antigravity_credential.rs: the login payload
  Antigravity.app and agy share, its go-keyring-base64 value, and the
  security command that writes the gemini/antigravity Keychain item with a
  15-second timeout.
- crates/quota-station-core/tests/antigravity_credential.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/antigravity_credential_tests.rs: the tests that
  a failed write keeps the old item and that a hung write is stopped before
  it can write late.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/desktop.rs
  from src-tauri/src/commands/account.rs and
  src-tauri/src/commands/system_config_types.rs: the version compare and the
  rule that Antigravity.app 2.0 and later keep their login in the Keychain.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/switch.rs
  from src-tauri/src/commands/account_desktop_switch.rs and
  prepare_account_for_injection in src-tauri/src/modules/account.rs: one
  switch at a time, the 60-second preparation (a fresh token and the
  project lookup through cloud_code.rs), quitting before and opening after,
  writing the login before the account pointers, and a reopen failure
  reported apart.

What was changed:

- macOS only. The Windows and Linux branches, the SQLite store (and with
  it switching Antigravity.app older than 2.0), the instance management,
  the WebSocket server, wake-up and the other platforms are not included.
- One OAuth client, read from a local oauth-client.json instead of
  constants in the source.
- Tokens are kept in the app's own macOS Keychain items instead of
  AES-encrypted files with their key beside them.
- A thread and blocking HTTP instead of async tasks and Tauri events; typed
  errors that keep no response body, token or secret; nothing about a login
  or a token is logged.
- Quota reads: no environment overrides, no autopush host, no onboardUser,
  no subscription tier or credit parsing (only the GCP ToS mark is read);
  loadCodeAssist only while a token lacks a project or the GCP ToS mark,
  and an answer without the mark is kept as no GCP ToS; a 429 or 5xx is
  not retried at once but waits longer before the next read; a quota
  summary that does not come back keeps the last full reading instead of
  caching one without it; the cache lives in the app's own folder.
- The pages the browser sees are translated to Vietnamese, error messages to
  English.
- Antigravity.app is quit with osascript and opened with open -b instead of
  closed by its process; it is never killed. The switch is checked with
  quota-axi afterwards, logged in the app's own folder, and watched for six
  hours for a running app writing its old login back. An Antigravity.app
  whose version cannot be read stops the switch instead of counting as new,
  and the index and the binding are written together or not at all.

A later milestone that adapts more of Cockpit Tools adds its parts to
this list.

