Adapted parts. Each file names its source in its header.

- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/keychain.rs
  from macos_keychain.py: the security commands, the read with -w and exit
  code 44 for a missing item, the write piped to security -i as hex, the
  command-line fallback for a long value and the 5-second limit.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/locks.rs
  from claude_locks.py: Claude Code's lock folders, their order and the
  proper-lockfile protocol.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/cc.rs
  from credentials.py, session.py and switcher.py: Claude Code's Keychain
  items (the default one and the one keyed to a CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR), the MCP
  and plugin secrets kept from the live login, and oauthAccount in
  ~/.claude.json.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/switch.rs
  from _perform_switch in switcher.py: the locks, the outgoing account's
  live login kept first, the target written, and everything put back when a
  step fails.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/usage.rs
  from oauth.py, usage_store.py and poll_policy.py: the usage and token
  endpoints, headers, client id and bodies, the reading of the windows, the
  error kinds, the expiry margin, the 180-second reuse and the back-off.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/session.rs
  from session.py (cswap run): the folder per account, its links to the
  owner's settings, the login variables removed from the environment, and
  a newer login taken back.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/manage.rs
  from cswap add and cswap add --token: a new login through claude auth
  login in a folder of its own, and a setup token kept as a credential.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/claude/import.rs
  from switcher.py and credentials.py: where claude-swap keeps each
  account's slot, oauthAccount and credential.

What was changed:

- The logins are in the app's own Keychain items
  (com.shin315.quota-station.claude), and its files hold no email and no
  token; a session's login goes to Claude Code's Keychain item for its
  folder, never to a file.
- A switch reads Claude Code's item and ~/.claude.json back and puts both
  back when they do not match, and writes nothing while claude-swap's own
  switchers are loaded.
- The account in use is read with Claude Code's live token and never
  refreshed by the app.
- The import only reads claude-swap's folder and Keychain items.

